 MLA Jacob Benson has chosen to join our party, sitting as a Farmer-Labour representative and has chosen to continue supporting the Cooperative Coalition. MLA Charles Agar has chosen to sit with the Grits. The remaining 3 MLAs have either joined the Conservative party or have retired from politics. 

 With the Progressives now out the picture, rural Saskatchewan seems ripe for the taking by our party. 

@pps_merge_yes
on-arrival: {!
    Q.pps_seats -= 5; 
    Q.ccf_ss_seats += 4; 
    Q.lps_seats += 1; 

    Q.central_d_pps_seats -= 2; 
    Q.central_d_ccf_ss_seats += 1; 
    Q.central_d_lps_seats += 1; 
    Q.southeast_d_pps_seats -= 2; 
    Q.southeast_d_ccf_ss_seats += 2; 
    Q.southwest_d_pps_seats -= 1; 
    Q.southwest_d_ccf_ss_seats += 1;
    window.updateBar('left');
    Q.ccf_ss_name = 'PFLP';
!}